      "message": "It will get caught, but then `var-\u003eInitializer()-\u003eType()-\u003eFriendlyName()` will segfault when it goes to add the error message, since Type() is null. I broke out specially instead of just doing a ternary -\u003eFriendlyName or \u0027undefined\u0027 to be explicit about ir::Function being special.\n\nIn general Type() is guaranteed to be not null here, except that ir::Function is a special case in CheckOperand, since it doesn\u0027t override the base -\u003eType().\n\n(Honestly the correct solution might be to add in a synthetic \u0027type::Function\u0027, so that ir::Function can return that and avoid the special case in CheckOperands, b/c I don\u0027t doubt this isn\u0027t handle correctly other places)",
